## Diagnostics before code changes

Follow **`no-guess-use-data.mdc`** and **`remote-log-first.mdc`**: remote logs, smoke (`test:anim-smoke`), `?animSmoke=1`, SSH, git, docs — not guesses.

## Terse or implicit failure signals

User intent may be **one word**, **one sentence**, a **screenshot**, or **implied** (“where is X?”, “still?”, “you didn't sync”). Do **not** require exact phrases like `debug`. If the arc of the conversation is “something should work and doesn't” → run **`terse-debug-ops.mdc`** and **`memory-bank/debug-ops-workflow.md`**: infer → logs → fix → verify → sync — same session.

## Memory + rules on session start (mandatory — NO EXCEPTIONS)

**Checklist A (8 steps)** every session/restart/compaction. **Checklist B** every turn. Includes **Read all alwaysApply `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`** (+ `~/.cursor/rules/` on DGX). Do not be lazy.

